+#### 3. Sign Convention Proposals for Deformed Exchange Relations
+
+We present two clear sign convention options for the deformed exchange relation:
+
+##### Option A: Literal Definition Convention (Recommended)
+Directly follows the exact formula in `docs/math/C_inhomogeneous_definition.md` (Definition 2.1):
+$$[b_j^s, a_1^\sigma] = - \mathrm{gb}_{\sigma, j, s} \cdot \kappa$$
+Equivalently, taking the commutator in standard fermion-first order:
+$$[a_1^\sigma, b_j^s] = + \mathrm{gb}_{\sigma, j, s} \cdot \kappa$$
+- **Pros**: 100% faithful to `docs/math/C_inhomogeneous_definition.md`. Mathematical papers and documentation need no sign adjustments.
+- **Form of deformation in bracket**:
+  When expanding composite bilinear generators $X = a_1^\sigma b_j^s$, the exchange of adjacent $b$ and $a$ operators picks up $-\mathrm{gb}_{\sigma, j, s}\kappa$.
+
+##### Option B: Positive Boson-First Convention
+Defines the commutator $[b_j^s, a_1^\sigma]$ with a positive sign:
+$$[b_j^s, a_1^\sigma] = + \mathrm{gb}_{\sigma, j, s} \cdot \kappa \iff [a_1^\sigma, b_j^s] = - \mathrm{gb}_{\sigma, j, s} \cdot \kappa$$
+- **Pros**: Matches some standard conventions where $[B, F] = + \mathrm{param}$.
+- **Cons**: Differs by an overall minus sign from `docs/math/C_inhomogeneous_definition.md`.
+
+> **Recommendation**: We recommend **Option A**, preserving strict consistency with `docs/math/C_inhomogeneous_definition.md`.
+
