+#### 4. Mathematical Computation of $\gamma_{abc}$ Coefficients
+The deformed Lie superalgebra bracket on composite bilinear generators is:
+$$[X, Y]_\gamma = [X, Y]_0 + \kappa \cdot \gamma(X, Y)$$
+where $[X, Y]_0$ is the undeformed graded commutator (Schema 1) and $\gamma(X, Y) = \sum_{c} \gamma_{abc} e_c$ is linear in the deformation parameters $\mathrm{gb}_{\sigma, j, s}$.
+
+Because all basis generators of $C(n+1)$ are bilinears of oscillators:
+1. **Odd generators**: $a_1^\sigma b_j^s$ ($4n$ generators).
+2. **Even generators**:
+   - $\mathfrak{sp}(2n)$ generators: $b_i^s b_j^{s'}$ ($2n^2 + n$ generators).
+   - $H_1 = a_1^+ a_1^- + b_1^+ b_1^-$ (contains the fermionic element $a_1^+ a_1^-$).
+
+**Non-zero $\gamma$ sectors**:
+- **Odd $\times$ Even**: When an odd generator $X = a_1^\sigma b_j^s$ is commuted with an even $\mathfrak{sp}(2n)$ generator $Y = b_k^t b_l^{t'}$, or with $H_1$, the reordering of operators yields $\kappa$ terms via $[b, a] = -\mathrm{gb} \cdot \kappa$. The resulting term is an odd generator multiplied by $\mathrm{gb} \cdot \kappa$.
+- **Odd $\times$ Odd**: When an odd generator $X = a_1^\sigma b_j^s$ is anticommuted with another odd generator $Y = a_1^{\sigma'} b_k^t$:
+  $$\{a_1^\sigma b_j^s, a_1^{\sigma'} b_k^t\} = a_1^\sigma b_j^s a_1^{\sigma'} b_k^t + a_1^{\sigma'} b_k^t a_1^\sigma b_j^s$$
+  Commuting $b_j^s$ past $a_1^{\sigma'}$ produces $-\mathrm{gb}_{\sigma', j, s} \kappa \cdot a_1^\sigma b_k^t$, which is an odd $\times$ odd correction yielding an even generator multiplied by $\mathrm{gb} \cdot \kappa$.
+- **Even $\times$ Even**: Purely bosonic $\mathfrak{sp}(2n)$ generators commute with each other with $\gamma = 0$. $H_1$ with $\mathfrak{sp}(2n)$ also has $\gamma = 0$.
+
+All computations will be performed symbolically using exact rational arithmetic via an extended `OscillatorPoly` engine that incorporates the inhomogeneous relation $b_j^s a_1^\sigma = a_1^\sigma b_j^s - \mathrm{gb}_{\sigma, j, s} \kappa$.
